+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | General Theory: Typed Architecture, Boundary, and Scope | What does the typed general theory claim, prove, and refuse? |
+| 2 | Theorem Atlas: Viability, Observation, Composition, Scale, Generation | Which theorem families are established, under which assumptions? |
+| 3 | Conserved Ledgers, Componentwise Diagnostics, Conservation–Viability Coupling | What do conservation laws buy for safety? |
+| 4 | Delay-Driven Institutional Dynamics: Hopf, Validated Folds, Cycle Stability | How do delayed channels generate cycles with certified facts? |
+| 5 | Sampled Governance, Closed-Loop Certification, Empirical Falsification | How can the theory be tested? |
+
+## Consolidation decisions (where the fewer-papers directive bites)
+
+- Paper 6 (A021 NAIM) folds into Paper 4's capstone by default
+- Paper 7 (stage/spatial) folds into Paper 4's supplement
+- Domain papers fold into Paper 5's single closed empirical case (G1)
+- E5's resource–sink admission serves Papers 3+5
+
+## Gap-filling agenda (G1–G6)
+
+G1: one closed empirical instantiation (top priority). G2: A021 coupling class. G3: continuum lift. G4: selector regularity. G5: external novelty audit. G6: TCS-1.1 freeze.
+
+## Release waves
+
+Wave 0: closure (G6, G5, manifests). Wave 1: Papers 1+2 (the theory dyad). Wave 2: Papers 4, 3, 5. Wave 3: the monograph.
